From f3c13c6e0320c1f8db5480c082d7fab2a64d8ce8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Martin Penkava <mpenkava1337@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 21:55:12 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] BD-J: start the JVM with -Xrs

HotSpot installs handlers for SIGINT, SIGTERM and SIGHUP when the VM is
created. They replace the handlers of the application that loaded
libbluray, and on such a signal the VM runs its shutdown and calls
exit() from one of its own threads while the application is still
running.

-Xrs keeps the VM away from these signals, as documented for embedded
VMs. Not passed to J2ME VMs.

Hades: only the context of the hunk is changed, to that of this tree,
where LibreELEC's 0001-set-headless-false.patch adds four lines after
-Xss2048k; the lines added are those of the commit. Here the JVM is
created only in the isolated BD-J host (hades-bdj-host), never in the
player's process, and that host installs no signal handlers: with -Xrs
a SIGTERM, SIGINT or SIGHUP of the service takes its default action and
ends the process at once, instead of the JVM running its shutdown
sequence (and the shutdown hooks a disc may have registered) and calling
exit() from one of its threads. The host already ends with _exit()
after a disc, which runs no hooks either.
---
 src/libbluray/bdj/bdj.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/libbluray/bdj/bdj.c b/src/libbluray/bdj/bdj.c
index 34f1a6e..21f930f 100644
--- a/src/libbluray/bdj/bdj.c
+++ b/src/libbluray/bdj/bdj.c
@@ -998,6 +998,11 @@ static int _create_jvm(void *jvm_lib, const char *java_home, BDJ_CONFIG *cfg,
     option[n++].optionString = str_dup   ("-Xms256M");
     option[n++].optionString = str_dup   ("-Xmx256M");
     option[n++].optionString = str_dup   ("-Xss2048k");
+#ifndef HAVE_BDJ_J2ME
+    /* Leave SIGINT, SIGTERM and SIGHUP to the application. Without -Xrs HotSpot installs its
+     * own handlers and calls exit() from a JVM thread while the application is running. */
+    option[n++].optionString = str_dup   ("-Xrs");
+#endif
     option[n++].optionString = str_dup   ("-Djava.io.tmpdir=/storage/.kodi/userdata/addon_data/tools.jre.zulu");
     BD_DEBUG(DBG_BDJ | DBG_CRIT, "Use /storage/.kodi/userdata/addon_data/tools.jre.zulu as cache dir.\n");
     option[n++].optionString = str_dup   ("-Djava.awt.headless=false");
